 [{:id :authority-boundary :status :sound-with-holds :detail "A pure 64-event, single-grant transient trace can compose synthetic data without asserting identity, owner consent, storage, external replay prevention, concurrency or native effect. A replayed whole trace can produce the same simulated result; no caller record is owner authority."}
  {:id :binding-and-deadlines :status :design-direction-sound :detail "Existing model:165-215 binds read release destination and entire copied release record at final comparison; model:112-129 exposes credential-not-after and approval/grant/release not-after. Plan:22-23 derives three write or four read deadlines and compares complete copied records; values are synthetic, not real tickets. Existing bound-p checks issued shape and matching IDs/digest but does not establish current issued-at or lifetime validity; composition must supply those checks."}
  {:id :totality :status :require-explicit-gate :detail "Plan:19,28,43 requires bounded acyclic validation of nested inputs before copy/equal, including malformed/cyclic data. Existing recursive copy at model:149-153 has no cycle guard; bounded validation must precede that helper and all snapshot comparisons, including mutated event input. Test exact maximum and maximum+1 event lengths and cyclic nested conses; no use of caller-supplied snapshots as trusted state."}
  {:id :translated-overflow :status :reachable :detail "For M=9007199254740991, prior=(M-10,10,10,t), current=(M-10,0,11,t), deadline=M, mono deadline=30: current latest=M-10<M; prior latest=M; monotonic delta=1 and lower-bound nonregression pass; translated prior upper=M+1 fails model:252-253. Add nearby positive with all earlier guards and overlap passing, and assert branch conditions as well as denial."}]
 :findings
 [{:id :f1-phase-and-storage-terminality :severity :must-specify-before-implementation :plan-lines [24 28 42 45]
   :finding "The grant status consumed is used both for a pending post-consume final and for an already completed, denied, restarted or otherwise canceled attempt. Grant status alone therefore cannot ensure one successful final, prevent final after restart, or preserve the different terminal behavior after a post-consume denial. Plan's storage failure/uncertainty wording also does not define the resulting internal phase, so a subsequent consume/final or revoke could be incorrectly admitted."
   :minimal-fix "Keep the existing externally modeled grant statuses, and define an internal non-authoritative phase/state such as pending-final versus closed, with explicit transition table: successful consume -> consumed/pending; final success or denial -> consumed/closed; restart or ticket loss after consume -> consumed/closed; pre-consume expiry -> invalidated/closed; failed or uncertain consume -> closed/unavailable with no ACK, no simulated effect and no retry, distinguishing known-not-committed from uncertain only if explicitly modeled. Revoke after consume returns already-consumed and does not itself count an effect; explicitly state whether it leaves a pending final unchanged, consistent with owner order, rather than implying revocation ACK. No actual durability claim."
   :synthetic-red "For each op assert issue/consume/final/final produces exactly one increment and second final denial; issue/consume/restart/final, issue/consume/failed-final/final and issue/consume/ticket-loss/final produce zero increments and consumed terminal; failed/uncertain storage followed by consume, final and revoke cannot produce success or ACK. Include consume/revoke/final in the declared ordering, with exact per-event outcomes and order."}
  {:id :f2-issue-time-relationships :severity :must-specify-before-implementation :plan-lines [22 23 31 41]
   :finding "Plan says 'check issued-at relationships' without defining them. Existing approval/grant/release validators only require issued-at < not-after (model:141-143), so a future-dated approval, grant or read release can otherwise be accepted even while the issue sample's latest is below all deadlines. The instruction to cap grant/approval validity is also ambiguous about release issue validity and the 60-second rule's reference point."
   :minimal-fix "Define conservative issue validity using the sampled UTC interval: each applicable record issued-at must be no later than the chosen defensible bound (use earliest for proof it is not future), issue latest strictly before each not-after, and approval before or at grant issue; define the exact issue-time maximum lifetime/cap rule consistently with V3 for approval and grant, preserve independently owned identity/release expiries, and reject inconsistent or overflowing arithmetic. Do not infer real owner provenance from these synthetic fields."
   :synthetic-red "Per read/write use future approval/grant issued-at and for read future release issued-at with otherwise fresh not-after; deny issue and zero counts. Include equality/boundary positive for a truly already-issued record, issue/grant ordering violations and safely capped lifetime/overflow cases."}]
